@startuml possession-flow-shot-selection
' ⚠ A DETAIL DIAGRAM. The whole possession, and the second-chance LOOP that
' this step sits at the TOP of, are in possession-flow.puml — read that first.
' ⚠ THIS FILE OWNS: who shoots, what kind of shot, and the putback weighting.
' ⚠ Notes say what the flow DOES; the argument lives in possession-flow-model.md.
' Render: plantuml -DPLANTUML_LIMIT_SIZE=16384 -tpng   (every diagram is now under
'   the 4096px default, so the flag is insurance — but keep using it, and ⚠ keep each
'   diagram SCREEN-SIZED: past ~2,000px it stops being readable long before it stops
'   rendering. ⚠ `-checkonly` does not lay out and does not catch deprecated syntax
'   that renders as a warning box — look at the PNG.)
title ShotSelector — who shoots, and what shot\n//§3.17 the shot mix · §3.22 the putback//

skinparam ActivityDiamondFontSize 11
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12
skinparam NoteFontSize 10

start
:read-and-clear the //putbackCandidate//
//set by whichever path just identified a rebounder//;
note right
  ⚠ **READ AND CLEARED IN ONE STEP, at the top of the iteration** —
  so a stale candidate is structurally impossible, and there is
   **NO decay across retentions**: the second putback in a
  possession is as likely as the first.
   **A rebounder is identified on THREE paths only** — the
  missed-shot board, the in-bounds block recovery, and the missed
  last free throw. The four other retention paths pass `null`
  and draw exactly as before.
end note

:**pick the shooter** — offensive-weight draw
//the putback candidate's weight ×  sim.offensive-rebounder-shot-weight//;
note right
   **The putback is a WEIGHT, not a branch** — there is no
  "is this a putback?" fork anywhere. Still **ONE** `nextDouble()`;
  only the boundaries move.
  ⚠ The RNG STREAM still moves: a different shooter takes a
  different branch, so downstream draws differ in meaning.
end note

:**pick the shot type** — per-type SHARE table
× avg-10 skill modifier of the shooter
//DRIVE / PERIMETER / POST / THREE  (sim.shot-share-*)//
//THREE × offensiveScheme lean · PERIMETER × its RECIPROCAL//;
note right
  One `nextDouble()`, four types.
   **Shot TYPE is not forced to the rim on a putback** —
  `pickShotType` bends by the shooter's own skills, so a big
  leans interior on his own.
  The lean split is the modern-vs-traditional axis: it moves the
  MIX per coach, not the league's three-point volume.
  ⚠ **A stopped shot charges NO FGA** (the foul branch returns
  before recordFieldGoalAttempt), and the three's foul multiplier
  is far below DRIVE's — so moving a draw to a three makes it far
  less likely to be stopped. **This path does NOT hold FGA constant.**
end note

:→ on to TurnoverResolver
//possession-flow.puml//;
stop
@enduml
